{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515213-shielding-spell-question","id":1515213,"title":"Shielding Spell Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-16T00:11:14-07:00","id":1515213,"title":"Shielding Spell Question","content":"Can a Mage make a Shielding spell that reduces damage? For example, based on the Matter 2 Alchemist's Touch rote, could a Mage create a similar spell with Forces 2, which would make them immune to bashing kinetic attacks and reduce Lethal by Potency? Or a Death spell that does the same effect but against most other attacks, as it shields against the target's very end? <br /> <br /> If so, then this would make Mages significantly more potent than I had previously imagined, however, it isn't necessarily outside of the range of possibility from my perspective. <br /> <br /> My only qualm is that under the Shielding practice it says &quot;Mages protect themselves from general harm through the power of their Arcana with the Mage Armor Attainment rather than Shielding spells.&quot; However, what is &quot;general harm?&quot; Is it just weapons (natural or otherwise)? In. which case a Mage immune to fire, which is specifically enumerated in the Shielding spell practice is immune to flamethrowers and other fire weapons. Is it any normal Attack, in which case Mages with Spirit shields can protect themselves from spirits' physical attacks. It seems arbitrary, and is likely just meant to convey that usually they use Mage Armor, since it's easy, reflexive, non-dispellable, and lasts a scene.<br /> <br /> What do you all think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26413-thatonekiasyd","name":"ThatOneKiasyd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26413_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T00:48:53-07:00","id":1515217,"title":"","content":"Shielding spells of an Arcanum protect the subject from specified sources of harm or invasion that fall within that Arcanum\u2019s purview. So yes, a Shielding Forces spell that deflects kinetic energy is doable.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure if I understood your third paragraph right, but in any case, when Mage Armor says you defend yourself from general harm, it means that you don\u2019t have to check for which source the damage comes from.<br /> Eg. Space Armor works fine against bullets.<br /> <br /> \u2026 Well okay that part isn\u2019t entirely accurate, since certain Arcana\u2019s Mage Armors do check for \u2018damage type\u2019. Just not whether they fall within the used Arcanum\u2019s purview.<br /> Eg. Mind Armor doesn\u2019t work on explosions, but the given rational is not \u201cOh, explosions are Forces\u201d, but because explosions don\u2019t have a mind for Mind Armor to scramble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T05:33:44-07:00","id":1515231,"title":"","content":"Shielding spells generally provides immunity (or at least CoW) against non-damaging hostile powers, and no-sell specific sources of damage. Mage Armour is for reducing incoming damage from more general sources.<br /> At least, this is the design philosophy.<br /> There's no explicit statement forbidding Shielding spells from acting as armour by reducing damage, but it's not intended, and it would easily make mage armour all but obsolete (except for situations where you need to activate it reflexively) since you can quite easily pump Potency about your Arcanum rating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T05:54:16-07:00","id":1515232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1515213-shielding-spell-question?p=1515231#post1515231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shielding spells generally provides immunity (or at least CoW) against non-damaging hostile powers, and no-sell specific sources of damage. Mage Armour is for reducing incoming damage from more general sources.<br /> At least, this is the design philosophy.<br /> There's no explicit statement forbidding Shielding spells from acting as armour by reducing damage, but it's not intended, and it would easily make mage armour all but obsolete (except for situations where you need to activate it reflexively) since you can quite easily pump Potency about your Arcanum rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, Forces is really the only Arcanum whose purview allows it to no-sell or mitigate kinetic damage, which is the overwhelming majority of non-magical damage sources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T06:21:26-07:00","id":1515234,"title":"","content":"Fate also works for mundane sources or to protect from specific dangers (protect a vampire from being set on fire or a changeling from falling to their death).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-16-2023, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T07:34:06-07:00","id":1515242,"title":"","content":"&quot;General harm&quot; is covered under the purview of what each of the mage armors covers. Shielding tends to be more for things that are not wizards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T08:46:03-07:00","id":1515251,"title":"","content":"Mage armour is an attainment and reflexive, so it is almost always more useful in the heat of the moment, putting together a shielding spell takes more time and preparation (and can be countered or dispelled) so you expect it to be more effective.<br /> <br /> Death to shield against dying wouldn't stop you taking damage but should prevent soul loss when you hit 0 health...<br /> <br /> Time shielding prevents you from bleeding out (or healing) and can make degenerate conditions pause.<br /> <br /> Mind/Spirit shielding against specific types of attacks using numina make perfect sense.<br /> <br /> Likewise Prime shielding against direct magical attacks, and Space shielding against being teleported into the Sun...<br /> <br /> I think most of these effect provide blanket immunity, which can be very potent. But not general damage prevention...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  typo 06-17-2023, 04:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T10:01:38-07:00","id":1515677,"title":"","content":"I'm not so restricting in my games. Forces Mage Armor grants a personal shield against damage, but there's no reason you can't cast a Kinetic Shield spell on your whole cabal that adds Potency-level Armor against kinetic attacks. Why not? It's under the purview of Forces. It takes a spell control slot of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}